 ```
 
+Footnotes are numbered and listed in the order in which they are first referenced
+in the document, regardless of the order in which they are defined. References
+made from within the content of other footnotes are numbered after all references
+in the body of the document. Footnotes which are defined but never referenced are
+listed last, in the order of their definitions. To number and list footnotes in
+the order of their definitions instead, set the `USE_DEFINITION_ORDER` option to
+`True`.
+
